    <heading level="1">Writing Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="532" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Why is there no real number equal to $$\sqrt{-64}?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="533" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the difference between $$9^{2}$$ and $$\sqrt{9}?$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary. 92 reads: “nine squared” and means nine times itself. The expression $$99$$ reads: “the square root of nine” which gives us the number such that if it were multiplied by itself would give you the number inside of the square root.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
